{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "#3 - Configure the user profile attributes with the Profile Editor",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Lab Overview",
      "description": "## Configure the user profile attributes with the Profile Editor\n\n 🎯 **Objective**    Add the additional attributes to the user profile so they can be added to the sign-up form.\n\n  🎬 **Scenario**     Algen Scoop Shop is opening launching a beta test of its new application. Users wil be required to enter an invitation code, which needs to be captured on the sign-up form. Before this field can be added to the sign-up form, it needs to be added as an attribute on the Okta user profile.\n\n  Since an invitation code is required to sign up, we'll make the attribute required. We'll also ensure that the invitation code can only be used once by marking the attribute as unique to each user. We'll also set the user permissions to Read-Write so that they can enter it into the sign-up form.\n"
    },
    {
      "title": "Add an additional required attribute",
      "description": "## Add an additional required attribute\n\n> Note: You should be logged in as your Super Admin user.\n\n1. From the Okta Admin Dashboard, select **Directory** > **Profile Editor**.\n\n2. Select **User (default)** row under the Profile column. \n\n1. In the Attributes section, select the **Add Attribute** button.\n\n1. In the attribute form enter the following values in the corresponding fields:\n    - Format: string \n    - Display name: Invitation Code\n    - Variable name: invite_code\n    - Description: Invitation Code for beta access\n    - Restriction: Value must be unique for each user \n    - Attribute length: Equals 6\n    - Attribute required: Yes\n    - User permission: Read-Write\n\n1. Select **Save**\n"
    },
    {
      "title": "Lab Checkpoint",
      "description": "## ✅ Checkpoint\n\nAt this point, you have updated the default User Profile and attribute permissions. Now you are ready to enable self-service registration for Algen Scoop Shop's new app!"
    }
  ]
}
